00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:40.750
There have been 7 different versions of the
Atom character total.

00:01:40.750 --> 00:01:42.049
And right now in the new 52 universe.

00:01:42.049 --> 00:01:47.120
The mantle of the Atom is being worn by a
woman named Rhonda Pineda.

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:55.000
The Ray Palmer version is still present in
the new 52 comics, but before the new 52 reboot

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:59.759
in Green Lantern Brightest Day he crossed
paths with Deathstroke who had killed the

00:01:59.759 --> 00:02:06.689
Ryan Choi version of the Atom.

00:02:06.689 --> 00:02:12.370
My favorite Ray Palmer story was actually
during Identity Crisis.

00:02:12.370 --> 00:02:15.970
That comic is looked down on a little for
doing some awful things to Sue Dinby, but

00:02:15.970 --> 00:02:20.520
Palmer's estranged wife Jean Loring ends up
using his Atom suit to shrink herself and

00:02:20.520 --> 00:02:22.510
accidentally kills Sue Dinby.

00:02:22.510 --> 00:02:25.640
She has this epic mental breakdown and gets
committed to Arkham Asylum and Palmer feels

00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:31.060
so guilty about the whole thing that he shrinks
himself so tiny no one can find him for years.

00:02:31.060 --> 00:02:42.020
When he went away is when the Ryan Choi character
took up the mantle using another one of Palmer's

00:02:42.020 --> 00:02:43.020
suits.

00:02:43.020 --> 00:02:47.860
It's a super dark story, so I'm guessing when
they say Routh's character has a 'dark past'

00:02:47.860 --> 00:02:53.560
it's going to have something to do with the
Sue Dinby character or it will be a twist

00:02:53.560 --> 00:02:55.500
on that.

00:02:55.500 --> 00:03:04.430
Here's the origin story of the Ray Palmer
character

00:03:04.430 --> 00:03:09.910
He was a physics professor at Ivy University
in New England and found a white dwarf star

00:03:09.910 --> 00:03:11.740
meteorite that landed on earth.

00:03:11.740 --> 00:03:15.390
He used that to make a lens that allowed him
to shrink himself down.

00:03:15.390 --> 00:03:20.860
During Zero Hour back in the 90s they rebooted
the character and he was turned into a teenage

00:03:20.860 --> 00:03:25.000
version of himself and found he was able to
shrink and grow himself without needing to

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:26.980
use the special lens he crafted from the meterorite.

00:03:26.980 --> 00:03:32.230
After that they changed the character again
so that he needed to use his tech to shrink

00:03:32.230 --> 00:03:33.990
and grow.

00:03:33.990 --> 00:03:38.810
But he started working with the Justice League
and teaching at Ivy Universty again.

00:03:38.810 --> 00:03:43.401
One of his students was Ronnie Raymond who
went on to become part of Firestorm.

00:03:43.401 --> 00:03:44.480
Remember in the comics, Felicity Smoak was
his stepmother.

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:47.530
I know on Arrow Ray Palmer is going to be
the new Felicity 'ship.

00:03:47.530 --> 00:03:55.090
But it's funny how their comic book characters
were connected too.

00:03:55.090 --> 00:03:59.900
Because of the events of Identity Crisis and
Palmer's wife murdering Sue Dinby, it created

00:03:59.900 --> 00:04:03.900
a lot of tension between Palmer and a lot
of the other Justice League members.

00:04:03.900 --> 00:04:04.960
Mostly Hawkman.

00:04:04.960 --> 00:04:07.871
He's not going to be featured on Arrow, but
I'm wondering if Brandon Routh's character

00:04:07.871 --> 00:04:10.290
